### 7. Check for errors  

All possible failure points are already guarded:

| Failure | Where it’s caught | What you’ll see |
|---------|-------------------|-----------------|
| ONNX file missing / 404 | Network panel, `loadOnnxModel` promise rejection | Red error box in `TestModelIntegration` + console error |
| Browser has no WebGPU and WASM fails | `ort.InferenceSession.create` → catch | Same red error box |
| `runModelBAnalysis` receives malformed history | Guard clause (`<4` entries) | Returns “Insufficient Data” payload (no crash) |
| Model‑B classifier sees only one class in test split | `try / catch` around `roc_auc_score` (Python) – not relevant at runtime; the ONNX model always outputs a probability (0‑1). | No error, just a probability value. |

If any of those errors appear, the red “❗️ Error:” line in the test component will show the exact message, and the console will contain the stack trace.

